irq_sim: dispatch with generic_handle_irq() when built as part of a module

irq_to_desc() is not exported to modules. Every simulated interrupt is mapped
with handle_simple_irq as its flow handler, so generic_handle_irq() runs the
same handler through the exported API. Only needed because this copy of
irq_sim.c is linked into gpio-sim.ko instead of the kernel (CONFIG_IRQ_SIM
is off in the OpenWrt armsr kernel).

--- a/irq_sim.c
+++ b/irq_sim.c
@@ -110,7 +110,7 @@
 				       work_ctx->irq_count, offset);
 		clear_bit(offset, work_ctx->pending);
 		irqnum = irq_find_mapping(work_ctx->domain, offset);
-		handle_simple_irq(irq_to_desc(irqnum));
+		generic_handle_irq(irqnum);
 	}
 }
 
